00:01:50.001 --> 00:01:54.000
Formations like these require
long hours of intensive

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:55.001
drilling and careful judgment.

00:01:56.001 --> 00:02:00.001
When the troop goes around the corner,
the riders on the outside of the turn have

00:02:00.001 --> 00:02:04.001
to adjust their speed to keep even
with the riders on the inside.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:09.001
The man on the outside has to ride
a lot farther and a lot faster

00:02:09.001 --> 00:02:11.000
in order to keep up with the parade.

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:18.001
The outside wheels must spin faster than
the wheels on the inside because they

00:02:18.001 --> 00:02:22.000
have a greater distance to travel
in the same length of time.

00:02:22.001 --> 00:02:28.000
When a wagon turns a corner, the wheels
can travel at different speeds because

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:30.001
each one can turn freely on the axles.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:36.000
And in the early automobiles,
the rear wheels turned separately and only one

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:38.000
wheel was connected to the engine.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:44.001
But when only one wheel was driven by the
engine, it had to do all the work and

00:02:44.001 --> 00:02:48.001
it couldn't get a good enough grip
on the road to do its job properly.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:51.001
So the one-wheel drive was soon out of date.

00:02:52.001 --> 00:02:57.001
But if two wheels are locked on an
axle so that they are not free to turn

00:02:57.001 --> 00:03:01.000
separately, one or the other has to slide.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:07.000
So engineers had to find a way to connect
both rear wheels to the engine without

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:09.000
sliding and slipping on turns.

00:03:09.001 --> 00:03:14.000
The device which makes this possible
is a part of the rear axle.

00:03:14.001 --> 00:03:19.000
It is called the differential
because it can drive the rear

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:21.000
wheels at different speeds.

00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:26.001
The differential looks complicated,
but once we understand its principle,

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:28.001
it is amazingly simple.

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:35.000
These two wheels are mounted on separate
axles and supported by a frame so that

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:38.001
they can revolve freely at different speeds.

00:03:39.001 --> 00:03:46.001
Let's fasten a spoke on the
inner end of each axle so that

00:03:46.001 --> 00:03:51.001
by turning the spokes,
we can turn each wheel separately.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:04:01.001
With a bar or cross piece,
we can turn both wheels in the same

00:04:01.001 --> 00:04:05.000
direction at the same rate of speed.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:09.001
Let's get something to hold
this bar in place so that it

00:04:09.001 --> 00:04:11.001
will press against the spokes.

00:04:12.001 --> 00:04:17.000
Notice that this support is not
locked to the axle. It turns freely.

00:04:18.001 --> 00:04:22.000
Now we can spin the wheels
by rotating the support.

00:04:23.001 --> 00:04:28.000
This is fine as long as both wheels
are able to turn at the same speed.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:32.001
But let's see what happens
when we go around the corner.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:38.000
With this arrangement, we cannot drive
one wheel faster than the other.

00:04:40.001 --> 00:04:45.000
And if we stop one wheel,

00:04:45.001 --> 00:04:48.000
the other wheel won't budge.

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:56.001
Let's put this bar on a pivot so that
it can swing in either direction.

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:08.000
Now, the bar can still turn
both wheels at the same speed.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:14.000
And because it pivots, it lets one wheel turn

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:16.001
even when the other is stopped.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:24.001
But if turned too far, the bar will swing
around until it won't drive the spokes

00:05:24.001 --> 00:05:26.000
that turn either wheel.

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:31.001
We need another crossbar and
more spokes to carry on the job.

00:05:32.001 --> 00:05:38.001
When we stop one wheel,
the crossbars will continue to push the spokes

00:05:38.001 --> 00:05:40.000
of the free wheel around.

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:48.000
As long as both wheels are free to turn,
the bars do not swing on their pivot

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:52.000
and the wheels move at the same speed.

00:05:53.001 --> 00:05:57.000
Now we have the working
principles of a differential.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:03.000
To adapt the model for use in an automobile,
we will have to make a few changes.

00:06:04.001 --> 00:06:11.000
In order to reduce the jerky action caused
by wide spaces between the spokes, we

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:12.001
will put in more spokes.

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:20.001
Further filling in the spaces
between the spokes gives

00:06:20.001 --> 00:06:23.000
steadier, more continuous action.

00:06:23.001 --> 00:06:28.000
And changing the shape gives firm,
constant contact.

00:06:29.001 --> 00:06:35.000
Now we can make the gears thicker and stronger,
and we have differential gears.

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:40.001
The edges are cut so that they will fit
together more smoothly and silently.

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:45.000
And another gear is added to
share the work of driving the

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:47.001
axles. The principle is the same.

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:54.001
In order to turn the support and drive
the wheels, we can fasten a large gear

00:06:54.001 --> 00:07:00.001
here, connected by a smaller
gear to a source of power.

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:12.001
Notice that the power is connected to
the differential at the center line.

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:19.001
We can make our model more compact
by moving the gears closer together.

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:25.000
When we put our differential in an automobile,
we have to leave room for the

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:28.000
drive shaft,
which carries the power from the engine.

00:07:29.001 --> 00:07:32.001
We may build the floor of the
car above the drive shaft.

00:07:34.001 --> 00:07:39.001
But if we do, we won't have much
room inside unless we make the

00:07:39.001 --> 00:07:41.000
top of the car high too.

00:07:42.001 --> 00:07:46.000
Of course we could lower the floor and ceiling,
but the drive shaft would be

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:49.001
higher than the floor.
This would have disadvantages.

00:07:50.001 --> 00:07:55.000
A shaft in the middle of the floor of
an automobile would be inconvenient for

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:58.001
passengers and would be
awkward for carrying luggage.

00:07:59.001 --> 00:08:04.000
Today, engineers have found a way to make
the car roomier and closer to the road

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:07.001
without a clumsy shaft above the floor.

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:14.000
The drive shaft from the engine to the
differential is lowered out of the way,

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:18.000
and the drive shaft is connected
to the rear axle at the bottom.

00:08:19.001 --> 00:08:25.000
A new low center drive makes the rear
axle quieter, stronger, and more durable

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:30.000
because it gives better,
smoother contact between the gears.

00:08:31.001 --> 00:08:38.000
The automobile of today with the low
center drive is stronger and more rugged.

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:45.000
Every part of the rear axle has been built
to withstand strains far greater than

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:48.001
it will ever meet on the
straightaway or around the corner.

00:09:19.001 --> 00:09:27.001
